# CastAdhan Portable — Telegram notification config (v1.8.0)
# ===========================================================
# Copy this to /etc/default/castadhan-telegram on the Pi, owner root, group
# castadhan, mode 0640 — so the castadhan service user can READ it but not
# modify it. e.g.:
#   sudo install -m 640 -o root -g castadhan this-file /etc/default/castadhan-telegram
# Fill in both values. With these set, the Pi sends:
#   • an immediate alert if any adhan FAILS to play
#   • a daily digest at 23:15 local: "all prayers fired today" or a warning
#
# Both are optional — with no token configured, all sends are silent no-ops
# and playback is completely unaffected.
#
# DO NOT commit the filled-in file. .gitignore excludes the live filename;
# only this .template (with empty values) belongs in version control.

# Bot token from @BotFather (looks like 123456789:ABCdef-XYZ...).
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=""

# Your numeric chat id (the chat between you and the bot). To find it:
#   1. set TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN above
#   2. send any message to your bot from your phone
#   3. POST /api/notify/detect_chat  → returns your chat_id
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=""
